posts.body:
I wrote a few things. I don't think that all of them count as mechanics but I wrote them anyway
- When the game denies access to its content for some reason. Like if you complete certain main quest then several sidequests become unavailable;
- Unskipable repetitive content (like a really long skill animation);
- Status cleaning item names that don't self explain themselves. Like when you get a status, are sure that you have an item to remove it but you have to look to the description of everything because you can't remember that an echo screen cures silence, for example;
- Main progress obtainable after boring obligatory minigames. Kinda like mass effect 2 probing planets;
- When the game is too punishing when you loose. Long backtrack from save to boss room, permanent losses and so on.
- Game content that is only obtainable through gacha or other random casino mechanics;
- Anything that messes your playthough at the end of the game. Like when you are 100 hours in a game and realizes that your skill build isn't good enough to beat the final boss so now what you should do? Redo all the game?
